From 3fab73f7370a3a0b853fdf1f126a33d091ab6b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Athul <athulkrishnan97@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:29:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] ASoC: samsung: add Exynos8895 ABOX driver and Galaxy Note
 8 card

ABOX is the Exynos8895 audio subsystem: DMAs, mixers and I2S/TDM ports
(UAIF), run by Samsung's Calliope firmware on a Cortex-A7 inside the
block. The driver loads calliope_{sram,dram,iva}.bin, maps them through
the ABOX SysMMU, boots the A7 and talks to it over the SRAM mailbox and
the ABOX GIC. Playback uses RDMA0 into the SPUS mixer, capture WDMA1 from
NSRC0, both programmed by the firmware over IPC.

Things the hardware needs that the downstream code doesn't make obvious:
- UAIF_CTRL0 bit 2 set makes the UAIF drive BCLK/LRCLK; getting it the
  wrong way round leaves both ends driving the clocks;
- the SPUS mixer must be flushed before a stream, or it free-runs;
- the firmware's CPU gear requests need an ABOX_CHANGED_GEAR answer
  before it records;
- the DMA position comes from the RDMA/WDMA status register.

The machine driver pairs UAIF0 with a CS47L93 codec as I2S clock
provider, its FLL running from the 26 MHz PMU clock output on MCLK1, and
caps the earpiece and headphone volumes below the point where they
clip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
